# Pairs with NoResurrection. The undo does not arm the resized copy to
# redirect (#4357), so after the swap back a router that cached the resized
# copy keeps reading it while a newer write lands on the old copy.
MODULE: NoResurrectionUndoLeavesResizedCopyServing
TARGET: NoResurrection
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the undo arms nothing on the resized copy, so a reader still on it is served a value the old copy has superseded
PERTURBS: UndoArm

--- FIND
    /\ alias = R
    /\ redir' = TRUE
--- REPLACE
    /\ alias = R
\* MUTATION: ArmRedirectsAsync arms nothing.
    /\ redir' = FALSE
--- END
